  "worked_solution": "The tangential component of acceleration is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{T}=\\frac{v\\cdot a}{||v||}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector and evaluating it at $t=1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,3{t}^{2}\u27e9 \\\\ v(1) & =\u27e8\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,3(1)^{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,3\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the acceleration vector by differentiating the velocity vector and it evaluating at $t=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,0,\\,6t\u27e9 \\\\ a(1) & =\u27e80,\\,0,\\,6(1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,0,\\,6\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $v(1)\\cdot a(1)$ and $||v(1)||:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1)\\cdot a(1) & =\u27e8\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,3\u27e9\\cdot \u27e80,\\,0,\\,6\u27e9 \\\\  & =18 \\\\ ||v(1)|| & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the tangential component of the acceleration at $t=1$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{T} & =\\frac{v(1)\\cdot a(1)}{||v(1)||} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangential component of the acceleration is $3\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{ms}}^{-2}.$",
